(7503984, 1195605, 77196, '<td valign="top">I''m sure that the score does not reflect the quality of the shot, which was primarily based on the DNMC''ers. Not sure how you give this a 1 even if it doesn''t meet the challenge. Beautiful reflections, sharp focus, great textures, Even added interest with the plant in its mouth. IMO, it deserved a 7 at least! <br/>Maybe the blue reflections took the perception of the head more towards brown than it would be otherwise. <br/>This shot makes me want to go shooting at that location!<br/>Thanks for sharing this great image.</td>', 'I''m sure that the score does not reflect the quality of the shot, which was primarily based on the DNMC''ers. Not sure how you give this a 1 even if it doesn''t meet the challenge. Beautiful reflections, sharp focus, great textures, Even added interest with the plant in its mouth. IMO, it deserved a 7 at least! Maybe the blue reflections took the perception of the head more towards brown than it would be otherwise. This shot makes me want to go shooting at that location!Thanks for sharing this great image.', '2017-03-06 08:45:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(7503986, 1195925, 77196, '<td valign="top">Phooey on the naysayers! This is a nice shot, and - at least to my eye - definitely pink. <br/>To my eye, what hurts this shot is a disconnect between the lighting and the main feature. For me, the main feature is the flower on the left (Western culture bias - reading left to right, plus it is closer and larger than the one on the right - both are directly facing the camera - the other pink blooms between are at an angle). However, the flower on the right is in full light, but the one on the left seems to be a bit of a shadow. <br/>I don''t find the pipe all that distracting, but I agree that it would be an improvement to crop off the clamp on the left (not all Minimal editing challenges allow cropping, but this one did). <br/></td>', 'Phooey on the naysayers! This is a nice shot, and - at least to my eye - definitely pink. To my eye, what hurts this shot is a disconnect between the lighting and the main feature. For me, the main feature is the flower on the left (Western culture bias - reading left to right, plus it is closer and larger than the one on the right - both are directly facing the camera - the other pink blooms between are at an angle). However, the flower on the right is in full light, but the one on the left seems to be a bit of a shadow. I don''t find the pipe all that distracting, but I agree that it would be an improvement to crop off the clamp on the left (not all Minimal editing challenges allow cropping, but this one did). ', '2017-03-06 08:54:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(7503987, 1195884, 77196, '<td valign="top">I think what hurt this shot score-wise is that people generally don''t like to see people out of focus. The sleeve is a nice bright red and in good focus. <br/>As I look at it, I think the composition works against it as well. It almost feels to me that it would work better if it was composed with right right side of the frame at the back of his head, and with more space in front of him - kind-of giving a space to "move" into... if that makes any sense.</td>', 'I think what hurt this shot score-wise is that people generally don''t like to see people out of focus. The sleeve is a nice bright red and in good focus. As I look at it, I think the composition works against it as well. It almost feels to me that it would work better if it was composed with right right side of the frame at the back of his head, and with more space in front of him - kind-of giving a space to "move" into... if that makes any sense.', '2017-03-06 08:58:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(7503989, 1195957, 77196, '<td valign="top">Wow! That''s a pretty neat effect, especially in minimal editing. <br/>I really like the arrangement, and the texture of the background. <br/>It seems to me that the bar codes visible on a couple of the items are REALLY distracting and take away the impact of the image.</td>', 'Wow! That''s a pretty neat effect, especially in minimal editing. I really like the arrangement, and the texture of the background. It seems to me that the bar codes visible on a couple of the items are REALLY distracting and take away the impact of the image.', '2017-03-06 09:02:23.000000', NULL, 0),
